-- A choice type declared under a § section. Its constructors are stored with
-- the section's path (`Part A.Red`), and the decoder used to compare the JSON
-- string with that, so "Red" matched nothing (smucclaw/l4-ide#947). Until
-- #1012 it then fell through to the untyped decoder and reached the
-- OTHERWISE below: every row answered FALSE with "status":"success".

§ `Part A`

DECLARE Colour IS ONE OF Red, Green, Blue

@export default Is it red
GIVEN c IS A Colour
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is red` c IS
  CONSIDER c
    WHEN Red THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

#EVAL `is red` Red
